+# Nestlancer v2.1 execution — PARTIAL checkpoint
+
+Date: 2026-10-14. Full requested scope remains 188 original proto HTML files / 181 ranked screenshot pairs. No scope reduction authorized. PUBLIC-FIRST BALANCED. Historical prompts will not run; historical reports remain untouched.
+
+## Baseline
+- Workspace `/home/user`; repository `/home/user/frontend-ui-upgrade`.
+- Branch `arena/27579574-frontend-ui-upgrade`; commit `5066dcade38c0bbb570576ffdca9a542b33b1665`; initial `git status --short` empty.
+- Initial workspace approximately 47 MB (including Git and original screenshots).
+- Reports, all screenshot trees, directory README files, and manifest present. P0 empty; skip. 188 original HTML, 181 ranked pairs, 82 distinct ranked paths.
+- Node/npm/Python available; search and fetch tools functional. Direct sandbox reference hosts blocked. Chromium installed through npm, dependencies/caches outside deliverables. Image tools available; original SVG chosen for compactness/control.
+- Chromium baseline captures: `evidence/baseline-*.webp`, 1440/390. Original mapped screenshots inspected via selective resized copies. Admin payment screenshot differs materially from existing fixture; do NOT replace fixture money/customer data to match it.
+- Baseline extraction excludes scripts/styles/comments and password values; resource.md not opened.
+
+## Reference contract / visual direction
+Warm paper, deep ink, brand teal, fine technical rules. Public pages pair editorial typography with original delivery-system illustrations, not floating generic SaaS boxes. Client calm and actionable; admin dense/opaque. No extra framework, no third-party runtime.
+
+| Ref | Pattern / traits observed | Rejected | Local adaptation / selector | Test |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| R1 | Magic UI animated beam connects system nodes | perpetual rainbow loop, React dependency | Home `.delivery-art`, original connected workflow scene and one-shot path | early/settled animation and reduced motion |
+| R2 | Aceternity Timeline: staged headings beside related content | scroll-linked sticky mega-layout | Services `.process-map`, sequential stages, native disclosure of existing deliverables | keyboard disclosure + mobile |
+| R3 | shadcn Dialog: inert background, close control | framework install | Payment `dialog[data-proto-dialog]` with named form, cancel, focus restoration | Escape, Tab, return focus |
+| R4 | GSAP matchMedia: cleanup when preference changes | GSAP payload | Native matchMedia lifecycle in proto-motion.js | live reduced preference change |
+| R5 | Hover.css: float / underline / icon forward vocabulary | bouncing, glow, repeated movement | scoped `.studio-v2 .btn`, `.work-cover` focus and hover | keyboard and touch equivalent |
+| R2/R5 | stages + restrained response | invented monthly billing control | Pricing `.engagements`, native FAQ and comparison anchors | exact prices, disclosures, navigation |
+
+## Exact first queue
+1. `proto/apps/landing/index.html`: split editorial/art hero, existing preview preserved below, distinct project covers.
+2. `proto/apps/landing/services/index.html`: process artwork, semantic service cards, native existing-feature disclosure.
+3. `proto/apps/landing/pricing/index.html`: price hierarchy, primary CTA, native FAQ, working comparison links.
+4. `proto/apps/web/login/index.html`: actual labeled form, show password button, explicit demo-only submission, quiet original art.
+5. `proto/apps/admin/payments/01a10a2c-2d0e-7499-b769-967d17a42197/index.html`: preserve conflicting fixtures visibly, money wrap, local action dialogs with no backend claims.
+Then portfolio landing and client projects to advance other lanes. Remaining routes stay NOT_STARTED, even when inheriting shared token/runtime changes.
+
+## QA strategy
+Static all-page links/IDs/labels/facts; browser changed pages 390/1440 light/dark, public 320/768/1920; screenshots selective. Motion early getAnimations, scroll, reduced/live change, no JS. Native interactions and axe, disclose unresolved inherited problems. Full screenshot-state verification remains independent of page testing.
+
+## Batch 2 executed — 2026-10-14
+The original first queue is historical, not a pending plan. Commit `cd09e90` was pushed and draft PR [#6](https://github.com/nestlancer/frontend-ui-upgrade/pull/6) opened after explicit authorization. Batch 2 continues that PR on the same branch.
+
+1. About: preserve studio story; original collaboration art, ordered workflow and value hierarchy.
+2. Landing Contact: preserve handoff to app form; original correspondence art, useful brief checklist and native FAQs. **No duplicate form.**
+3. Landing case-study template: preserve supplied Fintech/PayFlow facts; conceptual dashboard cover, section anchors, quote hierarchy.
+4. Landing blog listing: original local cards with editorial covers, accessible actual-data search/category controls; unavailable pagination/RSS disclosed.
+5. Landing article: original text/metadata, illustrative deployment sketch, linked contents, quiet reading body, nonpersistent preview reactions.
+6. App Contact: preserve current fields/options/defaults; native local-only validation, associated errors and explicit no-send behavior.
+
+Scoped optional `editorial.css` is wired only to these six pages; `studio.js` adds opt-in behavior. No framework, endpoint, duplicate route or build step. Reference R7 was fetched before edits; R2/R4/R5/R6 reused as documented in REFERENCE_RESEARCH.md.
+
+All nine landing routes now have substantive implementation. App Contact passes base-page QA but its screenshot field/default differs; exact state remains BLOCKED. See PROGRESS.md for cumulative counts and the precise next balanced queue.
+
+## Batch 3 executed
+The three mapped public web siblings and client inbox were upgraded independently (paths in `batch-3-paths.json`). Their unique content, defaults, metrics/comments/messages remain; new runtime is opt-in and local-only. Admin dashboard moves to the next batch rather than being counted as done. See PROGRESS.md for current 18-page coverage and explicit state mismatches. Full 188/181 scope remains unchanged.
