+    "CI caching, smaller artifacts, and service-level pipelines after monolith split. The team prioritized **operational ownership** while migrating on a Nestlancer-style stack—gateway at the edge, domain NestJS services, Prisma on Postgres, async work through RabbitMQ, and media on Backblaze B2. ## Where we started The team inherited single pipeline building every service on each commit. The triggering incident was clear: hotfix queue depth grew while waiting for unrelated image builds. Leadership funded the refactor when customer-visible latency and support load rose together—not when the diagram looked messy. ## Architecture before - Single deploy artifact coupling unrelated domains - Synchronous cross-module HTTP with partial timeouts - Mixed read/write traffic on one database primary - Ad-hoc file storage complicating virus scan and CDN caching ## Migration timeline ### Discovery · Strangler cutover · Reliability hardening · Stabilize and learn",
